; lcnc-suite, 2026-09-27 — the XYZAC example's M601. The bundled
; tool_length_probe/m601.ngc runs tool_touch_off, whose positioning and
; retracts are G53 moves. Under the xyzac TCP kinematics G53 addresses the
; kinematics' WORLD frame (the table-riding frame), so the toolsetter moves
; would land in the wrong place. This wrapper shadows the bundle's (first on
; SUBROUTINE_PATH): save the switchkins type, measure in identity, restore
; TCP. Under task the HAL pin is the truth; the preview parse has no HAL and
; reads the interpreter mirror #<_webui_kinstype> the 428/429 remaps keep.
; Identity in -> identity out. NOTE the XYZAC's remaps are the reverse of the
; TWP example's: here M429 selects identity and M428 TCP
; (xyzac-trt-kins sparm=identityfirst).
o<m601> sub
(WEBUI_SUB=m601) ;lcnc-suite: preview sub-span marker, silent in task
#<saved_kins> = 0
o100 if [EXISTS[#<_webui_kinstype>]]
  #<saved_kins> = #<_webui_kinstype>
o100 endif
o110 if [#<_task> EQ 1]
o111   if [EXISTS[#<_hal[motion.switchkins-type]>]]
         #<saved_kins> = #<_hal[motion.switchkins-type]>
o111   endif
o110 endif
o120 if [#<saved_kins> NE 0]
  M429                      ; identity kinematics for the G53 moves
o120 endif
#2000 = 0                 ; manual mode (measure the loaded tool)
o<tool_touch_off> call
o130 if [#<saved_kins> EQ 1]
  M428                      ; TCP again
o130 endif
(WEBUI_SUB_END) ;lcnc-suite: preview sub-span marker
o<m601> endsub
M2 (end program)
